":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"If we are doing the CCD then the shapes will be updated within integrate_forces by the lines below:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\n\tif (do_motion) { //shapes temporarily extend for raycast\r\n\t\t_update_shapes_with_motion(motion);\r\n\t}\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf we are not doing CCD then this PR will make do_motion false (whereas before it would still be true and shapes would be updated with motion in integrate_forces() ). So if we are not doing CCD then I have to update shapes in the traditional way within integrate_velocities via `_set_transform(new_transform, true)`.\r\n","created_at":"2026-10-05T09:21:09Z","updated_at":"2026-10-05T09:21:10Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124164#discussion_r4182456577","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124164","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/4182456577"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124164#discussion_r4182456577"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124164"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/4182456577/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":608,"original_line":608,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":4181894637,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":14,"position":14,"subject_type":"line"}]